---With a Filter, you can remove portions of data from a particular visual or view.
---@class aws.quicksight.Filter
---@field CategoryFilter? aws.quicksight.CategoryFilter A CategoryFilter filters text values.
---@field NumericRangeFilter? aws.quicksight.NumericRangeFilter A NumericRangeFilter filters numeric values that are either inside or outside a given numeric range.
---@field NumericEqualityFilter? aws.quicksight.NumericEqualityFilter A NumericEqualityFilter filters numeric values that equal or do not equal a given numeric value.
---@field TimeEqualityFilter? aws.quicksight.TimeEqualityFilter A TimeEqualityFilter filters date-time values that equal or do not equal a given date/time value.
---@field TimeRangeFilter? aws.quicksight.TimeRangeFilter A TimeRangeFilter filters date-time values that are either inside or outside a given date/time range.
---@field RelativeDatesFilter? aws.quicksight.RelativeDatesFilter A RelativeDatesFilter filters date values that are relative to a given date.
---@field TopBottomFilter? aws.quicksight.TopBottomFilter A TopBottomFilter filters data to the top or bottom values for a given column.
---@field NestedFilter? aws.quicksight.NestedFilter A NestedFilter filters data with a subset of data that is defined by the nested inner filter.
---@field HierarchyFilter? aws.quicksight.HierarchyFilter A HierarchyFilter filters data by drilling down through an ordered list of columns. Each level in the list narrows the data by one column, and the selected values at each level determine which values are available at the next.

