---@class aws.quicksight.GenerateEmbedUrlForAnonymousUserRequest
---@field AwsAccountId aws.quicksight.AwsAccountId The ID for the Amazon Web Services account that contains the dashboard that you're embedding.
---@field SessionLifetimeInMinutes? aws.quicksight.SessionLifetimeInMinutes How many minutes the session is valid. The session lifetime must be in [15-600] minutes range.
---@field Namespace aws.quicksight.Namespace The Amazon Quick Sight namespace that the anonymous user virtually belongs to. If you are not using an Amazon Quick custom namespace, set this to default.
---@field SessionTags? aws.quicksight.SessionTagList Session tags are user-specified strings that identify a session in your application. You can use these tags to implement row-level security (RLS) controls. Before you use the SessionTags parameter, make sure that you have configured the relevant datasets using the DataSet$RowLevelPermissionTagConfiguration parameter so that session tags can be used to provide row-level security.
---@field AuthorizedResourceArns aws.quicksight.ArnList The Amazon Resource Names (ARNs) for the Quick Sight resources that the user is authorized to access during the lifetime of the session.
---@field ExperienceConfiguration aws.quicksight.AnonymousUserEmbeddingExperienceConfiguration The configuration of the experience that you are embedding.
---@field AllowedDomains? aws.quicksight.StringList The domains that you want to add to the allow list for access to the generated URL that is then embedded. This optional parameter overrides the static domains that are configured in the Manage Quick Sight menu in the Amazon Quick Sight console. Instead, it allows only the domains that you include in this parameter. You can list up to three domains or subdomains in each API call.

---@class aws.quicksight.GenerateEmbedUrlForAnonymousUserResponse
---@field EmbedUrl distilled.Secret The embed URL for the dashboard.
