---@class aws.quicksight.GetDashboardEmbedUrlRequest
---@field AwsAccountId aws.quicksight.AwsAccountId The ID for the Amazon Web Services account that contains the dashboard that you're embedding.
---@field DashboardId aws.quicksight.ShortRestrictiveResourceId The ID for the dashboard, also added to the Identity and Access Management (IAM) policy.
---@field IdentityType aws.quicksight.EmbeddingIdentityType|string The authentication method that the user uses to sign in.
---@field SessionLifetimeInMinutes? aws.quicksight.SessionLifetimeInMinutes How many minutes the session is valid. The session lifetime must be 15-600 minutes.
---@field UndoRedoDisabled? aws.quicksight.Boolean Remove the undo/redo button on the embedded dashboard. The default is FALSE, which enables the undo/redo button.
---@field ResetDisabled? aws.quicksight.Boolean Remove the reset button on the embedded dashboard. The default is FALSE, which enables the reset button.
---@field StatePersistenceEnabled? aws.quicksight.Boolean Adds persistence of state for the user session in an embedded dashboard. Persistence applies to the sheet and the parameter settings. These are control settings that the dashboard subscriber (Amazon Quick Sight reader) chooses while viewing the dashboard. If this is set to TRUE, the settings are the same when the subscriber reopens the same dashboard URL. The state is stored in Amazon Quick Sight,...
---@field UserArn? aws.quicksight.Arn The Amazon Quick user's Amazon Resource Name (ARN), for use with QUICKSIGHT identity type. You can use this for any Amazon Quick users in your account (readers, authors, or admins) authenticated as one of the following:
---@field Namespace? aws.quicksight.Namespace The Amazon Quick Sight namespace that contains the dashboard IDs in this request. If you're not using a custom namespace, set Namespace = default.
---@field AdditionalDashboardIds? aws.quicksight.AdditionalDashboardIdList A list of one or more dashboard IDs that you want anonymous users to have tempporary access to. Currently, the IdentityType parameter must be set to ANONYMOUS because other identity types authenticate as Quick or IAM users. For example, if you set "--dashboard-id dash_id1 --dashboard-id dash_id2 dash_id3 identity-type ANONYMOUS", the session can access all three dashboards.

---Output returned from the GetDashboardEmbedUrl operation.
---@class aws.quicksight.GetDashboardEmbedUrlResponse
---@field EmbedUrl? distilled.Secret A single-use URL that you can put into your server-side webpage to embed your dashboard. This URL is valid for 5 minutes. The API operation provides the URL with an auth_code value that enables one (and only one) sign-on to a user session that is valid for 10 hours.
---@field Status aws.quicksight.StatusCode The HTTP status of the request.
---@field RequestId? aws.quicksight.String The Amazon Web Services request ID for this operation.

