---@class aws.quicksight.GetIdentityContextRequest
---@field AwsAccountId aws.quicksight.AwsAccountId The ID for the Amazon Web Services account that the user whose identity context you want to retrieve is in. Currently, you use the ID for the Amazon Web Services account that contains your Quick Sight account.
---@field UserIdentifier aws.quicksight.UserIdentifier The identifier for the user whose identity context you want to retrieve.
---@field Namespace? aws.quicksight.Namespace The namespace of the user that you want to get identity context for. This parameter is required when the UserIdentifier is specified using Email or UserName.
---@field SessionExpiresAt? string The timestamp at which the session will expire.
---@field ContextRegion? aws.quicksight.Region The region in which the context is to be used. Use this parameter to obtain an identity context for cross-region use.

---@class aws.quicksight.GetIdentityContextResponse
---@field Status aws.quicksight.StatusCode2 The HTTP status of the request.
---@field RequestId string The Amazon Web Services request ID for this operation.
---@field Context? string The identity context information for the user. This is an identity token that should be used as the ContextAssertion parameter in the STS AssumeRole API call to obtain identity enhanced Amazon Web Services credentials.

