---A HierarchyFilter filters data by drilling down through an ordered list of columns. Each level in the list narrows the data by one column, and the selected values at each level determine which values are available at the next.
---@class aws.quicksight.HierarchyFilter
---@field FilterId aws.quicksight.ShortRestrictiveResourceId An identifier that uniquely identifies a filter within a dashboard, analysis, or template.
---@field Column aws.quicksight.ColumnIdentifier The column that anchors the filter. This column determines the dataset that the whole filter applies to, so every column in HierarchyLevels and in HierarchyTree must belong to the same dataset.
---@field HierarchyLevels aws.quicksight.HierarchyFilterLevelList The ordered list of columns that defines the drill-down path of the filter. The first level is the top of the hierarchy. You can specify a maximum of 5 levels.
---@field HierarchyTree? aws.quicksight.HierarchyFilterNode The tree of selected values for the filter. Each node records the values that are selected at one level of the hierarchy, and its children record the selections beneath those values. Omit this attribute to define the drill-down path without restricting any values.
---@field NullOption aws.quicksight.FilterNullOption|string This option determines how null values should be treated when filtering data.
---@field MatchOperator aws.quicksight.HierarchyFilterMatchOperator|string Determines whether the values selected in HierarchyTree are kept or removed. Choose one of the following options:
---@field DefaultFilterControlConfiguration? aws.quicksight.DefaultFilterControlConfiguration The default configurations for the associated controls. This applies only for filters that are scoped to multiple sheets.

---A control from a hierarchy filter that displays the hierarchy as a dropdown list. You can expand a value to see and select the values beneath it, and select either a single value or multiple values.
---@class aws.quicksight.HierarchyFilterDropDownControl
---@field FilterControlId aws.quicksight.ShortRestrictiveResourceId The ID of the HierarchyFilterDropDownControl.
---@field SourceFilterId aws.quicksight.ShortRestrictiveResourceId The source filter ID of the HierarchyFilterDropDownControl. This must be the FilterId of a HierarchyFilter.
---@field Title? aws.quicksight.SheetControlTitle The title of the HierarchyFilterDropDownControl.
---@field DisplayOptions? aws.quicksight.HierarchyFilterDropDownControlDisplayOptions The display options of a control.
---@field Type? aws.quicksight.SheetControlListType|string The type of the HierarchyFilterDropDownControl. Choose one of the following options:
---@field CommitMode? aws.quicksight.CommitMode|string The visibility configuration of the Apply button on a HierarchyFilterDropDownControl.
---@field ControlSortConfigurations? aws.quicksight.ControlSortConfigurationList The sort configuration for the values displayed in the control. Only one sort configuration can be applied per control.
---@field ControlTitleFormatText? aws.quicksight.ControlTitleFormatText The title text format configuration for the control.

---The display options of a control.
---@class aws.quicksight.HierarchyFilterDropDownControlDisplayOptions
---@field TitleOptions? aws.quicksight.LabelOptions The options to configure the title visibility, name, and font size.
---@field InfoIconLabelOptions? aws.quicksight.SheetControlInfoIconLabelOptions The configuration of info icon label options.

