---@class aws.quicksight.StartAssetBundleExportJobRequest
---@field AwsAccountId aws.quicksight.AwsAccountId The ID of the Amazon Web Services account to export assets from.
---@field AssetBundleExportJobId aws.quicksight.ShortRestrictiveResourceId The ID of the job. This ID is unique while the job is running. After the job is completed, you can reuse this ID for another job.
---@field ResourceArns aws.quicksight.AssetBundleResourceArns An array of resource ARNs to export. The following resources are supported.
---@field IncludeAllDependencies? aws.quicksight.Boolean A Boolean that determines whether all dependencies of each resource ARN are recursively exported with the job. For example, say you provided a Dashboard ARN to the ResourceArns parameter. If you set IncludeAllDependencies to TRUE, any theme, dataset, and data source resource that is a dependency of the dashboard is also exported.
---@field ExportFormat aws.quicksight.AssetBundleExportFormat|string The export data format.
---@field CloudFormationOverridePropertyConfiguration? aws.quicksight.AssetBundleCloudFormationOverridePropertyConfiguration An optional collection of structures that generate CloudFormation parameters to override the existing resource property values when the resource is exported to a new CloudFormation template.
---@field IncludePermissions? aws.quicksight.Boolean A Boolean that determines whether all permissions for each resource ARN are exported with the job. If you set IncludePermissions to TRUE, any permissions associated with each resource are exported.
---@field IncludeTags? aws.quicksight.Boolean A Boolean that determines whether all tags for each resource ARN are exported with the job. If you set IncludeTags to TRUE, any tags associated with each resource are exported.
---@field ValidationStrategy? aws.quicksight.AssetBundleExportJobValidationStrategy An optional parameter that determines which validation strategy to use for the export job. If StrictModeForAllResources is set to TRUE, strict validation for every error is enforced. If it is set to FALSE, validation is skipped for specific UI errors that are shown as warnings. The default value for StrictModeForAllResources is FALSE.
---@field IncludeFolderMemberships? aws.quicksight.Boolean A Boolean that determines if the exported asset carries over information about the folders that the asset is a member of.
---@field IncludeFolderMembers? aws.quicksight.IncludeFolderMembers|string A setting that indicates whether you want to include folder assets. You can also use this setting to recusrsively include all subfolders of an exported folder.

---@class aws.quicksight.StartAssetBundleExportJobResponse
---@field Arn? aws.quicksight.Arn The Amazon Resource Name (ARN) for the export job.
---@field AssetBundleExportJobId? aws.quicksight.ShortRestrictiveResourceId The ID of the job. This ID is unique while the job is running. After the job is completed, you can reuse this ID for another job.
---@field RequestId? aws.quicksight.NonEmptyString The Amazon Web Services response ID for this operation.
---@field Status aws.quicksight.StatusCode The HTTP status of the response.

---@class aws.quicksight.StartAssetBundleImportJobRequest
---@field AwsAccountId aws.quicksight.AwsAccountId The ID of the Amazon Web Services account to import assets into.
---@field AssetBundleImportJobId aws.quicksight.ShortRestrictiveResourceId The ID of the job. This ID is unique while the job is running. After the job is completed, you can reuse this ID for another job.
---@field AssetBundleImportSource aws.quicksight.AssetBundleImportSource The source of the asset bundle zip file that contains the data that you want to import. The file must be in QUICKSIGHT_JSON format.
---@field OverrideParameters? aws.quicksight.AssetBundleImportJobOverrideParameters Optional overrides that are applied to the resource configuration before import.
---@field FailureAction? aws.quicksight.AssetBundleImportFailureAction|string The failure action for the import job.
---@field OverridePermissions? aws.quicksight.AssetBundleImportJobOverridePermissions Optional permission overrides that are applied to the resource configuration before import.
---@field OverrideTags? aws.quicksight.AssetBundleImportJobOverrideTags Optional tag overrides that are applied to the resource configuration before import.
---@field OverrideValidationStrategy? aws.quicksight.AssetBundleImportJobOverrideValidationStrategy An optional validation strategy override for all analyses and dashboards that is applied to the resource configuration before import.

---@class aws.quicksight.StartAssetBundleImportJobResponse
---@field Arn? aws.quicksight.Arn The Amazon Resource Name (ARN) for the import job.
---@field AssetBundleImportJobId? aws.quicksight.ShortRestrictiveResourceId The ID of the job. This ID is unique while the job is running. After the job is completed, you can reuse this ID for another job.
---@field RequestId? aws.quicksight.NonEmptyString The Amazon Web Services response ID for this operation.
---@field Status aws.quicksight.StatusCode The HTTP status of the response.

